<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  floppy's Intuition stage (the reference abilities/cognition/intuition with the
  TypeSafe processor): the fast System 1 pick, made by the decision service
  (never by a free-text model) over the turn's choices, with the original's
  self-tuning confidence gate. The cognition (abilities/cognition/cognition.scx)
  invokes it once per turn after autonomy left the turn unhandled.

    deciding (an invoked decision service) -> done

  Processor (the original providers/typesafe Processor.process, the decision
  service's kind select): the turn's choices, the <param> choices (the
  body's assembled snapshot choices: its own enabled event:schema
  transitions and each ability's latest offers, tagged with the offering
  ability as target; the reference collect_offered_events), less the deliberate
  handoff bot.ability.reasoning.input (the processor never offers it), go
  to the decision service with the state document {turn: {envelope: {name},
  data}} (the original _stimulus_document) and the stimulus data as evidence. It
  asks one batch over them plus its pass criterion __unhandled__, filling
  each event's required data from the stimulus data's value, else the
  schema's enum; an event it cannot fill is not offered, so a reply that
  needs free text goes on to reasoning (user answer, 2026-10-08). When the
  pass criterion wins (declined) or nothing could be filled (no-candidates)
  the product is empty: the turn escalates with the original's reason
  empty_product and the tuner observes nothing. Otherwise the service
  returns every groundable event, each with its data and its own
  probability (decision.selected): the original's selections with their
  per-event confidences.

  Confidence (the reference ConfidenceTuner, 0-100 scale): the tuner state
  {mean, var, n} comes in as a <param> and goes back in <donedata>, so
  it lives in the cognition across turns. The turn's confidence is the
  minimum of its selections' confidences, each its probability normalized
  to a whole 0-100 number (the reference selection_confidence,
  normalize_confidence). <decision:tuner> observes it first, then writes
  the updated threshold (the original's defaults: the floor 35 during the warmup
  of 8 observations, then max(floor / 2, mean - k_sigma * std); EMA alpha
  0.08, variance floor 100) as a probability, and the turn escalates when
  the confidence is below it (the original _tune_confidence, should_escalate).

  Classification (the original _classify_activity, its confidence_gate off, the
  default): a confident product is handled, every selection {event, data}
  (escalation reason none), which the body routes to the target offering
  each (the original dispatches each to its single enabler). A low-confidence
  product (low_confidence), or one holding bot.ability.reasoning.input
  (deliberative_input), is unhandled and escalates to reasoning, but hands
  out its environment actions first: its selections less the deliberate
  handoff and bot.ability.cognition.ignore (the original _environment_actions),
  as selected in the donedata, which the cognition routes before
  reasoning's own selections. The decision timer is deciding.after
  (floppy's own bound; the original's intuition has none).

  Dispatch (the original _dispatch_selections_activity,
  cognition.types.dispatch_selected_events): the selections handed out are
  checked before the stage answers: <bot:verdict> removes ignore
  selections and applies attention_selection_error with the turn's focus
  and focus_candidates, then <decision:route> places each on the target
  offering it in the choices. One that cannot be placed fails the stage
  with the original's "Selection rejected: <message>". The original first re-asks its
  processor once with the rejection as feedback (routing_rejection); the
  decision service takes no such feedback, so that retry is not ported.

  Output: <donedata>, received by the cognition as done.invoke.intuition:

    {turn, handled: true, selected: [{event, data}], reason: "none", tuner}
    {turn, handled: false, selected: [{event, data}], reason, tuner}
                                          (escalate to reasoning)
    {turn, handled: false, failed: true, reason, tuner}

  A rejected selection,
  decision.failed, error.*, or no answer within decision_timeout_ms fails
  the stage (the cognition answers the turn with bot.ability.failed); the
  cognition's hop timeout bounds the whole stage too.

  Bindings: the bot namespace package, and the decision namespace and
  service packages, resolved from their repository URIs; env scopes TYPESAFE_API_KEY and TYPESAFE_BASE_URL to the
  service's <invoke> (without a key it answers decision.failed
  unconfigured). An invoked service's events are not checked against
  event:schema (scxml.rs checks only events between SCXML sessions): the
  decision service validates every selection's data against the choices'
  schema for it before returning it, and its own events are shape-checked
  by cond (Object(...) reads a non-object as {}).
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:bot="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/bot"
       xmlns:decision="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/namespaces/decision"
       xmlns:env="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/env"
       xmlns:event="https://github.com/stateforward/scxml.rs/namespaces/event"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" name="intuition" initial="deciding">
  <datamodel>
    <!-- The turn, from the cognition's <param>s. -->
    <data id="turn" expr="0"/>
    <data id="stimulus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus" expr="null"/>
    <data id="focus_candidates" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="choices" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="tuner" expr="({mean: 70, var: 100, n: 0})"/>
    <data id="decision_timeout_ms" expr="20000"/>
    <data id="instructions" expr="'You decide what a small companion robot does with one stimulus it observed. Choose the offered event the robot should take for it. Abstain when none of them fits, so slower reasoning handles it.'"/>
    <!-- The decision in flight. -->
    <data id="stimulus_data" expr="({})"/>
    <data id="confidence" expr="null"/>
    <data id="threshold" expr="null"/>
    <data id="decision_timer" expr="null"/>
    <data id="result" expr="null"/>
    <data id="failed_code" expr="null"/>
    <!-- The selection being dispatched, and why it was rejected (null when
         placed). -->
    <data id="dispatch_selections" expr="[]"/>
    <data id="rejection" expr="null"/>
  </datamodel>
  <script src="intuition.js"/>

  <state id="deciding">
    <onentry>
      <assign location="stimulus_data" expr="stimulusData()"/>
      <send idlocation="decision_timer" event="deciding.after" delayexpr="decisionTimeoutDelay()"/>
    </onentry>
    <onexit>
      <cancel sendidexpr="decision_timer"/>
    </onexit>
    <invoke id="decision" type="https://github.com/stateforward/floppy/services/decision"
            env:apikey="TYPESAFE_API_KEY" env:baseurl="TYPESAFE_BASE_URL">
      <param name="kind" expr="'select'"/>
      <param name="choices" expr="processorChoices()"/>
      <param name="state" expr="decisionState()"/>
      <param name="data" expr="stimulus_data"/>
      <param name="instructions" expr="instructions"/>
    </invoke>

    <!-- The decision service's own events. Every groundable event, each
         with its own confidence: observe their minimum, then compare it
         with the updated threshold. -->
    <transition event="decision.selected" cond="hasSelections(_event)" target="done">
      <assign location="confidence" expr="selectionConfidence(_event)"/>
      <decision:tuner location="tuner" thresholdlocation="threshold" observe="confidence"/>
      <log label="intuition" expr="tunedLog(_event)"/>
      <if cond="isLowConfidence()">
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('low_confidence', _event)"/>
      <elseif cond="hasDeliberativeInput(_event)"/>
        <assign location="result" expr="escalatedResult('deliberative_input', _event)"/>
      <else/>
        <assign location="result" expr="selectionResult(_event)"/>
      </if>
      <bot:verdict location="dispatch_selections" rejectionlocation="rejection" selections="result.selected"
                   focus="focus" candidates="focus_candidates"/>
      <if cond="isAccepted()">
        <decision:route location="dispatch_selections" rejectionlocation="rejection" selections="dispatch_selections" choices="choices"/>
      </if>
      <if cond="isRejected()">
        <assign location="result" expr="rejectedResult()"/>
      </if>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.abstain" cond="isAbstainReason(_event)" target="done">
      <log label="intuition" expr="abstainedLog(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="abstainedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="decision.failed" target="done">
      <assign location="failed_code" expr="failedCode(_event)"/>
      <assign location="result" expr="decisionFailedResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="deciding.after" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="timedOutResult()"/>
    </transition>
    <transition event="error.*" target="done">
      <assign location="result" expr="couldNotRunResult(_event)"/>
    </transition>
    <!-- The service ended without an answer: the timer decides. -->
    <transition event="done.invoke.decision"/>
  </state>

  <final id="done">
    <donedata>
      <content expr="result"/>
    </donedata>
  </final>
</scxml>
